Below is a simple script example that denies access to a website or service. This script is written in JavaScript and can be used on a web server to redirect users to a "denied access" page or display a message.

### JavaScript (Client-Side)
```javascript
// Check if the user is allowed to access the page
function checkAccess() {
    const allowedUsers = ["user1", "user2"]; // List of allowed users
    const currentUser = "user3"; // Replace with actual user authentication logic

    if (!allowedUsers.includes(currentUser)) {
        alert("Access denied! You are not authorized to view this page.");
        window.location.href = "/access-denied.html"; // Redirect to denied access page
        return false;
    }
    return true;
}

// Call the function when the page loads
window.onload = checkAccess;
```

### Server-Side (Node.js with Express)
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();

// Middleware to check access
function checkAccess(req, res, next) {
    const allowedUsers = ["user1", "user2"]; // List of allowed users
    const currentUser = req.session.user; // Assuming user is stored in session

    if (!allowedUsers.includes(currentUser)) {
        return res.status(403).send("Access denied! You are not authorized to view this page.");
    }
    next();
}

// Protected route
app.get('/protected', checkAccess, (req, res) => {
    res.send("Welcome to the protected page!");
});

// Access denied route
app.get('/access-denied', (req, res) => {
    res.status(403).send("Access denied! You are not authorized to view this page.");
});

// Start the server
app.listen(3000, () => {
    console.log('Server is running on port 3000');
});
```

### HTML (Access Denied Page)
Create a simple HTML page to display when access is denied:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Access Denied</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Access Denied</h1>
    <p>You are not authorized to view this page.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

### Notes:
1. **Authentication**: Replace the placeholder user authentication logic with your actual authentication mechanism (e.g., JWT, OAuth, session-based auth).
2. **Security**: For production environments, ensure that sensitive checks are performed server-side to prevent tampering with client-side code.
3. **Customization**: Customize the error message, redirect URL, and styling as needed for your application.

This script can be adapted to various programming languages and frameworks depending on your stack.
